@startuml agentic-value-stream-measurement-dimensions
' Per CR-VAS-005 §4 (Measurement Architecture) + §35 (Operational Value Assessment).
' Cardinal author rule: Emmanuel A. Otchere <emmanuel@otchere.com>
' Last revised: 2026-10-08.

title Agentic Value Stream ; Six Primary Measurement Dimensions

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false

rectangle "Value Realization\n(PRIMARY)" as VR #LightYellow {
}

rectangle "Agentic\nEffectiveness" as AE #LightBlue {
}

rectangle "Decision &\nAction Quality" as DQ #LightBlue {
}

rectangle "Human\nIntervention" as HI #LightGreen {
}

rectangle "Authority\n& Risk" as AR #LightPink {
}

rectangle "Operational\nEfficiency" as OE #LightGray {
}

VR --> AE : informs
AE --> DQ : informs
DQ --> HI : informs
HI --> AR : informs
AR --> OE : informs
VR --> OE : informs

note right of VR
  Primary dimension. Measures
  whether agentic participation
  improves the intended Value
  Stream outcome.
end note

note right of HI
  Human intervention is
  measured as a dimension,
  NOT automatically as failure.
end note

note right of AR
  Authority utilization is
  diagnostic, NOT inherently
  positive. Boundary compliance
  is critical.
end note

@enduml
